// Regiment types. Compiled into the asset pack by gc_bake; the game never
// reads this file directly.
//
// models: soldiers at full strength (at most 32). files: soldiers per rank
// when raised; ranks follow from models / files. speed: tiles per second.
// turn_rate: degrees per second. file_spacing, rank_spacing: tiles between
// neighbouring soldiers across and front to back.
//
// Melee: a blow lands with chance 50 + melee_attack - the target's
// melee_defence percent (kept between 10 and 90) and takes melee_damage hit
// points. Each front-rank soldier strikes once a second. charge_bonus is extra
// melee damage, percent, when a charge hits home; it fades over 3 seconds.
// ranged: range in tiles, damage per arrow, seconds between volleys, and the
// percent of arrows that hit a block of normal density.
//
// morale: how much a regiment can take before it breaks and runs, 1 to 100
// (it wavers below 25 and routs at 0; see docs/05-combat.md). Units that
// fight to the last say never_routs: true instead.
//
// Weapon room (docs/05-combat.md): mass is Light (swarms), Medium (the
// default) or Heavy (cavalry, monsters); it decides who gives ground when
// lines crush together. reach: true for spears and pikes (the second rank
// fights too, at half weight, and they strike at once when lines meet).
// swing_room: true for big swinging weapons (cramped in Tight order, no
// defence lost in Loose). shield: true lets a regiment form a shield wall.
// discipline: true gives the Clans' Formation Discipline (+15% of its melee
// defence standing still in Tight order or a shield wall; a roster unit has it
// from its "Formation Discipline" ability). All of them are off unless written.
//
// points: what the regiment costs from a Field Battle army's points budget
// (Skirmish 2,000, Battle 4,000, Grand Battle 8,000; docs/06-game-modes.md).
// Every regiment costs 400 for now, so a Battle army is ten regiments, the
// size the balance pass below was tuned at.
//
// Numbers are first-pass, tuned so the factions' Field Battle armies are
// close to even (docs/17-unit-rosters.md, "Field Battle balance").
